\DOC ASSERT_CONCL_TAC

\TYPE {ASSERT_CONCL_TAC : term -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Checks that the goal's conclusion is the supplied term, leaving the goal
unchanged.

\DESCRIBE
Takes a term {t : term} to be compared against the goal's conclusion. It yields
exactly one subgoal identical to the input goal, the conclusion returned
unaltered and no assumptions added or removed; it is thus an identity step
whose only role in a proof script is to assert that the conclusion is {t}.
{
        A ?- t
     ============  ASSERT_CONCL_TAC t
        A ?- t
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces only this single outcome occurs, and only on goals with
no assumptions whose conclusions are existentially quantified specification
statements.

\ENDDOC
